# 1. PROJECT VISION AND OBJECTIVES

EmotiSound is a browser-based speech emotion recognition platform that analyzes a voice recording and predicts which emotion category best matches its acoustic patterns.

A user should be able to upload a recording, listen to it, inspect its waveform and spectrogram, run a trained deep learning model, view predicted emotion probabilities, explore acoustic characteristics, and review the analysis history.

The platform should explain the model's output in a technically meaningful but accessible way.

For example, a user uploads a recording of someone saying a sentence. The application processes the audio, extracts a log-Mel spectrogram, passes it through a trained convolutional neural network, and returns a prediction such as "Happy" or "Sad", together with the probability distribution across all supported classes.

The output represents the model's learned classification of vocal patterns. It must never claim to establish a person's actual internal emotional state.

## Primary objectives

1. Implement a genuine deep learning model using PyTorch.
2. Use a recognized speech emotion dataset, preferably RAVDESS.
3. Build a reproducible preprocessing, training, validation, and testing pipeline.
4. Evaluate the model using appropriate classification metrics.
5. Provide a fully functional web application with a polished, professional interface.
6. Visualize the audio signal and its time-frequency characteristics.
7. Integrate the trained model with the backend for real inference.
8. Include a model evaluation and training-results section.
9. Make the project easy to install, run, demonstrate, and explain.
10. Keep the system modular so individual components can be improved later.

The application must not be a collection of static screens. Every major feature must be connected to working functionality.

